{% comment %}
  Tilet rule — the woven border of the netela, reduced to three thin lines.

  DESIGN_LANGUAGE §6b: maximum 4px tall. The three lines sit flush against each
  other (1px each, 3px total) — the moment this gets thick it stops reading as a
  woven edge and starts reading as a flag.

  Usage:
    {% render 'tilet-rule' %}
    {% render 'tilet-rule', width: '120px' %}
    {% render 'tilet-rule', width: '100%', class: 'my-divider' %}
{% endcomment %}

<span
  class="tilet{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
  style="--tilet-width: {{ width | default: '72px' }};"
  {% unless animate == false %}data-animate="fade"{% endunless %}
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <i class="tilet__line tilet__line--green"></i>
  <i class="tilet__line tilet__line--gold"></i>
  <i class="tilet__line tilet__line--red"></i>
</span>
